## Corrected Claims

### CORRECTION-A · United Airlines market share (Footnote 4)
**Draft language:** "United flies roughly 68% of its departures"  
**Footnote as drafted:** "United ≈68% of flights; next carrier ≈4%"  
**Problem:** Live fetch of the Simple Flying source ("Washington Dulles' 5 Largest Airlines by Market Share") returned 70.42% for United and 5.12% for Delta. The evidence record E-0009 cited 68% and 4%, misreading or reading an earlier version of the article. The evidence record's caveat acknowledged the need to "confirm against MWAA air traffic statistics."  
**Correction applied:** Body changed to "roughly 70%"; Footnote 4 updated to "United ≈70% of flights; next carrier ≈5%." The corrected figures strengthen the single-carrier concentration argument.

### CORRECTION-B · Gate count in master plan (Footnote 3)
**Draft language:** "a fifth runway, and 24 new gates"  
**Problem:** Live fetch of the ffxnow.com master plan article (E-0079's source) confirmed "gate expansion from the current 130 to 218 gates by 2080–2090, representing an 88-gate increase." The evidence record E-0079 stated "24 more gates," which does not appear in the source article and cannot be traced to any other evidence record. This is a source-integrity failure in the evidence brief.  
**Correction applied:** Body changed to "88 new gates"; Footnote 3 updated to "88-gate expansion from 130 to 218 gates by 2080–2090."

### CORRECTION-C · Footnote 11 — "Grant Assurance 29(C)"
**Draft language:** "the prior-federal-investment interest Grant Assurance 29(C) and Section 163(C) protect"  
**Problem:** Grant Assurance 29 concerns Airport Layout Plan compliance; it has no "(C)" subpart. The "(C)" notation belongs only to Section 163 (the three-prong test), not to GA 29. Applying "(C)" to GA 29 is a citation error.  
**Correction applied:** Footnote 11 changed to "Grant Assurance 29 and Section 163(C) protect."

