## Source-Integrity Problems

### SI-01 — Evidence record E-0009 misread its source
The evidence record `airline-commercial-strategist::E-0009` cited "United operates 68% of the flights at the airport, with Delta Air Lines a very distant second at just 4%." The underlying Simple Flying article now shows 70.42% and 5.12% respectively. Whether the article was updated after the brief was compiled or whether the brief misread the data, the source does not support the 68%/4% figures used in the draft. Corrected in the final draft as noted in CORRECTION-A.

### SI-02 — Evidence record E-0079 misread its source
The evidence record `chief-engineer::E-0079` extracted "24 more gates" from the ffxnow.com master plan article. The article does not contain this figure. The correct figure from the article is 88 additional gates (from 130 to 218). Corrected in the final draft as noted in CORRECTION-B.

### SI-03 — E-0068 acre count (not in final draft)
E-0068 (LandApp blog) states "433 acres" for the Western Lands sale, contradicting the MWAA primary source (E-0001, E-0019, E-0090) which consistently says 424 acres. The draft correctly used 424 acres from the primary MWAA source; E-0068 is rated "disputed" in the ledger. No correction needed to the draft.

